# A TestFlight Test Room build compiles these public values into its JS bundle.
# `npm run test-room:publish` writes the real 90-day values to the ignored
# `.env.test-room-build`; do not paste a short-lived or silently clamped token.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CRAYS_TEST_BUILD=1
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CRAYS_TEST_ROOM_SERVICE_URL=https://crays-test.relays.nuts.cash
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CRAYS_TEST_ROOM_INVITE_TOKEN=<public-broadcast-invite>
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CRAYS_TEST_RELAY_URL=wss://crays-test.relays.nuts.cash
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CRAYS_TEST_ROOM_ID=crays-test-room
# Optional: point a development device at the relay-only compatibility proxy.
# It never handles invites. Start it with: CRAYS_TEST_ROOM_PROXY=1 npm run test-room
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CRAYS_TEST_RELAY_URL=ws://192.168.1.20:8787
# Comma-separated public transport relays used only for NIP-46 signer discovery.
# A pasted bunker:// link continues to use the relays declared by that signer.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CRAYS_NIP46_RELAYS=wss://relay.nsec.app
# Hosted Stripe checkout defaults to the shared Nuts payment service. QA may
# replace this at Metro bundle time with a deterministic checkout adapter.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_PAYMENT_SERVICE_URL=https://payments.nuts.cash
